 • Today, I completed an exciting piece of work that’s been on my radar for a while — integrating custom rate limiting algorithms into my Spring Boot REST API service.

 • This was done in order to learn about the little nuances of various Rate Limiting algorithms, gain flexibility and exercise control over how API rate limits are enforced at the backend.

 • I had built a separate project to experiment with and implement various rate limiting strategies.

 • Today, I packaged that project as a dependency and plugged it into my Spring Boot service via 𝘏𝘛𝘛𝘗 𝘧𝘪𝘭𝘵𝘦𝘳𝘴 — enabling fine-grained control over API traffic.

