 1. Packaged my rate-limiter project as a dependency and published to maven local

 2. Included the dependency in my gradle spring boot service
 
 3. Spun up a redis container

 4. Created a HTTP Filter to intercept the incoming HTTP Requests and tied up the requests to check for api request rate limitin

 5. If the desired rate limit is not breached, continue with the request

 6. Else, return a structured error response with error message - "𝗧𝗼𝗼 𝗺𝗮𝗻𝘆 𝗿𝗲𝗾𝘂𝗲𝘀𝘁𝘀. Please try later" with a HTTP status code of 429

